## Auth

API key, sent as `Authorization: Bearer {{ENV_VAR_NAME}}` on every
request via a single `apiRequest()` wrapper. Proven by
`github-mcp-server`, `postgres-mcp-server` (connection-string variant),
and `stripe-mcp-server` in the original catalog.

**Before you rely on the Bearer-header assumption**, check your
provider's actual token-exchange/request docs — it's not universal.
Notion, for example, needed Basic-auth + JSON instead; see the OAuth
head's notes for a worked example of a provider that broke this exact
assumption.

Use the most tightly scoped key/token your provider offers — never a
default full-access key if a restricted/read-only one is available.
